body:
When I edit my process.json

```
{
  "apps" : [{
    "name"        : "push",
    "script"      : "./index.js",
    "watch"       : false,
    "merge_logs"  : true,
    "env": {
      "DEBUG": "cofactories-push:*",
      "NODE_ENV": "production"
    }
  }]
}
```

stop watching directory ,pm2 can start my json ,but if I restart the process and start watching ,God daemon crashed

I declare app name `app` I can start , but when I run `pm2 delete push` or `pm2 kill`, pm2 daemon will crash

part of my .json file

```
{
      "name": "push",
      "script": "./server.js",
      "log_date_format": "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm Z",
      "instances": 1,
      //or 0 => 'max'
      "min_uptime": "200s",
      // 200 seconds, defaults to 1000
      "max_restarts": 15,
      // defaults to 15
      "max_memory_restart": "200M",
      // 1 megabytes, e.g.: "2G", "10M", "100K", 1024 the default unit is byte.
      "cron_restart": "1 0 * * *",
      "watch": false,
      "ignore_watch": [
        "[\\/\\\\]\\./",
        "node_modules"
      ],
      "merge_logs": true,
      "exec_interpreter": "node",
      "exec_mode": "cluster",
      "autorestart": false,
      // enable/disable automatic restart when an app crashes or exits
      "vizion": false,
      // enable/disable vizion features (versioning control)
      "env": {
        "NODE_ENV": "development",
        "PORT": 8883
      }
    },
```
